Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:24:57 +0000
Subject: Use origin-keyed processes by default

Enable the OriginKeyedProcessesByDefault feature. Every origin that does
not opt out with the "Origin-Agent-Cluster: ?0" response header gets an
origin-keyed agent cluster and a renderer process locked to that origin,
so pages from different subdomains of one site never share a process.
This build already isolates every site and enables strict origin
isolation, which places each http and https origin in its own process, so
the number of renderer processes does not change in practice. The feature
keys those processes by origin rather than by a site URL that happens to
be an origin, which is how upstream intends per-origin isolation to work,
and it keeps per-origin processes if strict origin isolation is turned off
in chrome://flags. GrapheneOS Vanadium uses the same default.

